From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 16:30:00 -0700
Subject: cam: csid: keep RDI as packed passthrough on pre-480 CSIDs

The IFE hw mgr enables RDI crop+drop unconditionally at acquire ("CSID
will enable only for ver 480 HW", but nothing enforces that). The CSID
format lookup uses crop||drop as "rpp", and for a MIPI RAW N -> RAW N
RDI that flips the decode format from payload passthrough (0xf, packed)
to plain16 unpacking (0x3). On Titan 170 (sdm845) the RDI then writes
16-bit-per-pixel rows (2688 B/row for the binned 1344-wide OS04C10)
into a buffer userspace sized for packed RAW12 (2016 B/row): the write
overflows the buffer (CAMNOC SLAVE_IRQ / SMMU faults) and the BPS reads
misaligned bayer, producing a frame repeated 3x horizontally with a
dead band at the bottom. Legacy 4.9 forces crop off for payload-only
RDI paths. Do the same on pre-480 HW: when in_format == out_format,
disable crop/drop so the RDI stays packed passthrough.
---

--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/isp_hw_mgr/isp_hw/ife_csid_hw/cam_ife_csid_core.c	2026-07-02 16:08:11.905574495 -0700
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_isp/isp_hw_mgr/isp_hw/ife_csid_hw/cam_ife_csid_core.c	2026-07-02 16:08:11.915574468 -0700
@@ -2618,6 +2618,26 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The hw mgr enables RDI crop/drop unconditionally, but only ver 480
+	 * class CSIDs implement RDI pixel processing (rpp). On older CSIDs
+	 * (e.g. Titan 170 / sdm845) passing rpp to the format lookup switches
+	 * a MIPI RAW passthrough (decode fmt 0xf, packed) to plain16 unpacking
+	 * (decode fmt 0x3): the RDI then writes 16-bit-per-pixel rows into a
+	 * buffer userspace sized for packed data, overflowing it (CAMNOC/SMMU
+	 * faults) and feeding the BPS misaligned bayer. Match the legacy 4.9
+	 * behaviour: payload-only passthrough with crop/drop disabled.
+	 */
+	rc = cam_cpas_get_cpas_hw_version(&camera_hw_version);
+	if (rc)
+		camera_hw_version = 0;
+	if ((camera_hw_version != CAM_CPAS_TITAN_480_V100) &&
+		(camera_hw_version != CAM_CPAS_TITAN_175_V130) &&
+		(path_data->in_format == path_data->out_format)) {
+		path_data->crop_enable = false;
+		path_data->drop_enable = false;
+	}
+
 	rc = cam_ife_csid_get_format_rdi(path_data->in_format,
 		path_data->out_format, &path_format, &plain_fmt, &packing_fmt,
 		path_data->crop_enable || path_data->drop_enable, &in_bpp);
